<BaseLayout
  title="Why this works — Acquira"
  description="The research behind Acquira's lessons and reviews, in plain terms."
>
  <h1>Why this works</h1>
  <p>
    Acquira is built on research into how people learn languages. Here is what that means for you.
  </p>
  <h2>Lessons that are just a little harder</h2>
  <p>
    Each lesson builds on the last. Linguist Stephen Krashen called this "i+1": input you mostly
    understand, plus a little new.
  </p>
  <h2>Words come back just before you forget them</h2>
  <p>
    Reviews use spaced repetition (the SM-2 algorithm): the better you know a word, the longer until
    you see it again.
  </p>
  <h2>Recalling beats re-reading</h2>
  <p>
    You try to remember before the answer appears. Typing the answer makes you produce it, which
    researchers call the generation effect.
  </p>
  <h2>Easy on the brain</h2>
  <p>Audio and text together, nothing extra to distract you — cognitive load theory in practice.</p>
</BaseLayout>
